t-108-cli-for-ready-editions
build a sript in python
it will work as a cli
i will start it
it will prompt me for a link
i will provide a link
it checks if the link
startswith "https://wolnelektury.pl/media/book/txt/"
and endswith "txt"
it will open and fetch the text
first line is the author following the Format: first name, last name
the script splits into name and surname and asks the user to confirm - user can accept, edit or cancel everything
next is a blank line
next line - one or more - is the title, it may come into many lines until the next blank line
the script fetches is asks the user to confirm just as before - user can accept, edit or cancel everything
next, sometimes comes ISBN, but not always. We skip it
next, the script asks the user for the year. user need to copy it from another source by hand
next comes the body of the work. 
on the bottom of each page there is a footnote section
it always starts with fee blank lines followed by:
"""
-----
Ta lektura, podobnie jak tysiące innych, dostępna jest na stronie wolnelektury.pl."""
That is: five dashes, newline and the sentence "Ta lektura, podobnie jak tysiące innych, dostępna jest na stronie wolnelektury.pl."
the work ends before the 5 dashes so we ignore everythin that comes after - and ignore the empty lines in between.
The text is saved as ExternalEdition instance
next, every word as ExternalEditionSpelling
 





